>
	<h2>Raymond Solomon</h2>

	<p>
		<strong>Senior Financial Advisor</strong> with 20 years of experience
		following and analyzing global financial markets.
	</p>

	<p>
		My approach is built around understanding market structure, economic
		data, earnings, and the factors that can move prices across different
		asset classes.
	</p>

	<h2>Experience & Education</h2>

	<p>
		Over two decades of market experience have given me exposure to a wide
		range of financial conditions, from major economic cycles to periods of
		extreme market volatility.
	</p>

	<p>
		I studied at <strong>London Business School (LBS)</strong>, with a focus
		on finance and the principles that underpin modern financial markets.
	</p>

	<h2>Markets I Follow</h2>

	<ul>
		<li>Stocks & Equities</li>
		<li>Commodities</li>
		<li>Forex</li>
		<li>Precious Metals</li>
		<li>Cryptocurrency</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Market Experience</h2>

	<p>
		My work focuses particularly on understanding the events and market
		conditions that can create significant opportunities or risks.
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Earnings Season:</strong> analyzing company results,
			expectations, guidance, and market reactions.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Non-Farm Payrolls (NFP):</strong> following employment data
			and its potential impact on currencies, commodities, and equities.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Equity Markets:</strong> identifying potential opportunities
			during periods of heightened volatility.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		One notable example from my market experience was identifying Tesla
		around the $300-per-share level during the COVID-era market environment.
		Market opportunities like this demonstrate why preparation, discipline,
		and understanding the broader market context matter.
	</p>

	<h2>My Approach</h2>

	<p>
		I believe successful market analysis starts with preparation rather than
		prediction. Economic releases, company earnings, price action, and
		market sentiment all need to be considered together.
	</p>

	<p>
		The objective is not to chase every move in the market. It is to identify
		high-quality setups, understand the risks involved, and make decisions
		based on a clear process.
	</p>

